# Expectation record for 04_bitfields/001_layout_and_size.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_layout_and_size
area               = 04_bitfields
description        = Bitfield size, alignment and byte image for fully covered allocation units
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every bitfield is declared on an explicit unsigned int or signed int base type, so its
signedness is stated by the program rather than chosen by the implementation, and the
allocation unit is four bytes on all four targets.  A byte image is printed only for
structs whose every bit is covered by a named field, so no unspecified padding bit is ever
observed; the struct that necessarily leaves padding is read back only through its named
members.  Each union is read through the member last written, so no type punning is
relied upon.  Every stored value is masked to its destination field's exact width, so no
store is out of range.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
sizeof_packed3=4
alignof_packed3=4
sizeof_oneword=4
alignof_oneword=4
sizeof_withsigned=4
alignof_withsigned=4
sizeof_spanning=8
alignof_spanning=4
sizeof_covered32=4
alignof_covered32=4
packed3_readback a=5 b=21 c=300
oneword_readback lo=4660 hi=22136
oneword_image 34 12 78 56
covered32_readback a=1 b=12345 c=101 d=678
covered32_image 73 e0 b2 a9
volatile_packed3_readback a=5 b=21 c=300
volatile_oneword_readback lo=4660 hi=22136
volatile_oneword_image 34 12 78 56
volatile_covered32_readback a=1 b=12345 c=101 d=678
volatile_covered32_image 73 e0 b2 a9
END
